### What is the factual origin of the "Pizzagate" conspiracy theory, and have fact-checkers or official investigations verified its claims?
Answer: The "Pizzagate" conspiracy theory originated on 4chan in 2016, wheretrolls analyzing John Podesta's hacked emails (released by WikiLeaks) seized on innocuous references to "cheese pizza"—a phrase that happened to be 4chan-internal slang for child pornography—and fabricated claims that Comet Ping Pong restaurant in Washington, D.C., was a front for a child sex-trafficking ring run by Hillary Clinton, Podesta, and other Democrats. No fact-checkers or official investigations have verified the theory's claims; the source notes that "to date, no evidence or victims have come forward to confirm the existence of a crime of any sorts at Comet Ping Pong," the restaurant doesn't even have a basement, and the theory was instead identified by the Senate Intelligence Committee (via testimony from Clint Watts) as part of Russian "Active Measures" online operations, while the FBI designated it a domestic terrorism threat in 2019.

Source URL: https://rationalwiki.org/wiki/Pizzagate

