### Justification
The claim is entirely unsubstantiated. Comet Ping Pong, the pizzeria at the center of the so-called "Pizzagate" conspiracy, does not even have a basement ([The Cut](https://www.thecut.com/2016/12/to-understand-pizzagate-it-helps-to-understand-cults.html)), and the theory itself originated on 4chan in 2016 from misinterpreted WikiLeaks emails, later identified by the Senate Intelligence Committee as part of Russian "Active Measures" ([RationalWiki](https://rationalwiki.org/wiki/Pizzagate)). No credible law enforcement investigation has ever substantiated any involvement by Hillary or Bill Clinton in a child sex-trafficking ring ([FactCheck.org](https://www.factcheck.org/2019/06/headlines-twist-old-report-on-state-department/), [USA Today](https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/factcheck/2020/06/21/fact-check-hillary-clinton-wasnt-court-testifying-june-2/3199725001/)), and no indictments, convictions, or victim testimony have ever emerged ([PolitiFact](https://www.politifact.com/factchecks/2020/oct/07/facebook-posts/four-years-later-theres-still-no-evidence-support-/), [Lead Stories](https://leadstories.com/hoax-alert/2020/09/fact-check-pizzagate-is-not-real.html)). The D.C. police officially called Pizzagate a "fictitious online conspiracy theory," and the man who fired an assault rifle inside the restaurant to "self-investigate" pleaded guilty and conceded, "The intel on this wasn't 100 percent" ([Lead Stories](https://leadstories.com/hoax-alert/2020/09/fact-check-pizzagate-is-not-real.html)).